        "Attributes": [
          {
            "Id": 758315,
            "attributeType": "LongString",
            "attributeName": "AIDescription",
            "attributeRelationType": "None",
            "Value": "The Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES), also known as the Super NES or simply SNES, is a 16-bit home video game console developed and marketed by Nintendo. Released as the Super Famicom in Japan in 1990, it arrived in North America in 1991 and internationally throughout 1992. A successor to the NES, the SNES engaged in a fierce \"console war\" with Sega's Genesis, pushing the boundaries of graphics and sound with features like Mode 7 and ADPCM audio. \n\nThe SNES boasted advanced capabilities, including compatibility with enhancement chips like Super FX, and a controller with added buttons. It achieved immense success, selling over 49 million units and delivering iconic titles such as *Super Mario World*, *The Legend of Zelda: A Link to the Past*, *EarthBound*, *Super Metroid*, and *Chrono Trigger*.  Even today, it remains popular among collectors and retro gamers, with numerous rereleases and emulations available."
          },
